49 247 649 249C649 256 644 257 628 257C611 257 611 257 606 240C582 153 511 73 433 41C404 30 378 24 350 24C302 24 263 36 232 58C180 92 156 141 156 222C156 232 156 243 157 251C165 327 193 421 226 479C266 550 325 604 395 634C432 649 474 659 510 659C601 659 651 591 651 481Z\"></path></defs></svg>","mathFallback":false,"description":"JEE Main's 2004 AIEEE 2004 Paper's All Questions with solutions provider ExamSIDE.Com","paperTitle":"AIEEE 2004","nextq":"Ayp9esSeCFh069MM","prevq":"xnMc4pIlDWh0AoYp","questions":[{"country":"in","examGroup":"jee","question_id":"izv8S3XrstKy7Chw","exam":"jee-main","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"subjectGroup":null,"subject":"chemistry","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","languages":["en"],"chapter":"basics-of-organic-chemistry","year":2004,"paperTitle":"AIEEE 2004","difficulty":"easy","topicName":null,"type":"mcq","examDate":null,"question":{"en":{"content":"Which of the following compound is not chiral? ","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"1- chloropentane"},{"identifier":"B","content":"3-chloro-2- methyl pentane "},{"identifier":"C","content":"1-chloro -2- methyl pentane "},{"identifier":"D","content":"2- chloropentane "}],"correct_options":["A"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.131ex\" height=\"1.507ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -666 500 666\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> - chloropentane is not chiral while others are chiral in nature\n<br><br><img class=\"question-image\" src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/o3fULOXNVTTegyINr/P4WB5FCVkSZNGRHnURaQ7BQPkikGc/wjzZVEAzHDPHSybZYEc2cH/image.png\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"AIEEE 2004 Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 286 English Explanation\"> "}},"permalink":"which-of-the-following-compound-is-not-chiral-2004-marks-4-izv8s3xrstky7chw.htm","timeAllotted":120000,"paperId":"aieee-2004","topic":"isomerism","isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":["odd_one_out"],"yearKey":"aieee-2004","active":true},{"country":"in","examGroup":"jee","question_id":"pe3VuSMjafKGXbUY","exam":"jee-main","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"subjectGroup":null,"subject":"chemistry","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","languages":["en"],"chapter":"hydrocarbons","year":2004,"paperTitle":"AIEEE 2004","difficulty":"medium","topicName":null,"type":"mcq","examDate":null,"question":{"en":{"content":"Which one of the following has the minimum boiling point?","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"n-butane"},{"identifier":"B","content":"isobutane"},{"identifier":"C","content":"1- butene "},{"identifier":"D","content":"1- butyne "}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<b>NOTE :</b> Among isomeric alkanes, the straight chain isomer has higher boiling point than  the branched chain isomer. The greater the branching of the chain, the lower is the boiling point. Further due to the presence of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> electrons, these molecules are slightly polar and hence have higher boiling points than the corresponding alkanes. \n<br><br>Thus <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.93ex\" height=\"1.984ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 2179 877\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D435\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D435\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(759,0)\"><use data-c=\"2E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1037,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D45D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1540,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D461\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D461\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1901,0)\"><use data-c=\"2E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> follows the order\n<br><br>alkynes <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.09ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.312ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -540 778 580\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"3E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> alkene <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.09ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.312ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -540 778 580\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"3E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>  alkanes (straight chain) &gt; branched chain alkanes. "}},"permalink":"which-one-of-the-following-has-the-minimum-boiling-point-2004-marks-4-pe3vusmjafkgxbuy.htm","timeAllotted":120000,"paperId":"aieee-2004","topic":"properties-and-preparation-of-alkanes","isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":[],"yearKey":"aieee-2004","active":true},{"country":"in","examGroup":"jee","question_id":"mo99S4jYeBTUH1NS","exam":"jee-main","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"subjectGroup":null,"subject":"chemistry","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","languages":["en"],"chapter":"basics-of-organic-chemistry","year":2004,"paperTitle":"AIEEE 2004","difficulty":"medium","topicName":null,"type":"mcq","examDate":null,"question":{"en":{"content":"Consider the acidity of the carboxylic acids:<br>\n(a)  PhCOOH <br>\n(b) o – NO<sub>2</sub>C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>4</sub>COOH <br>\n(c) p – NO<sub>2</sub>C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>4</sub>COOH<br>\n(d) m – NO<sub>2</sub>C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>4</sub>COOH <br>\nWhich of the following order is correct?","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"(b) &gt; (d) &gt; (a) &gt; (c)"},{"identifier":"B","content":"(b) &gt; (d) &gt; (c) &gt; (a)"},{"identifier":"C","content":"(a) &gt; (b) &gt; (c) &gt; (d)"},{"identifier":"D","content":"(b) &gt; (c) &gt; (d) &gt; (a)"}],"correct_options":["D"],"answer":null,"explanation":"In aromatic acids presence of electron withdrawing substituent e.g. <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.483ex\" height=\"1.932ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -704 2865.6 854\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D441\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D441\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(1666,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(796,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> disperses the negative charge of the anion and stablises it and hence increases the acidity of the parent benzoic acid.\n<br><br>Further <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.726ex\" height=\"1.643ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -704 763 726\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>- isomer will  have higher acidity than corresponding <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.986ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 878 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45A\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.138ex\" height=\"1.439ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 503 636\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45D\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> isomers.  Since nitro group at <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.138ex\" height=\"1.439ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 503 636\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45D\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>-position have more pronounced electron withdrawing than <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.483ex\" height=\"1.932ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -704 2865.6 854\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D441\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D441\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(1666,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(796,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> group at <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.986ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 878 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fil